  message: "v6.0.0 RELEASE-BLOCKING SECURITY ARC — scope, PR sequence, deps (agent, 2026-06-08)\n\nCONTEXT. 344 commits since v5.0.1 + a 7-version schema jump (0.5.8->0.13.0, incl. breaking canonical_name removal) make a 6.0.0 release overdue. But the Unreleased section newly promotes the per-entry-point safety-claims feature + auto-generated SECURITY.md to the front door, while this cluster shows that feature currently asserts FALSE guarantees. Decision: gate 6.0.0 on this arc only (false-CONFIRM + no-op-scan + network-leak items). Other P0s (stable_id, JS zero-edges, etc.) ship as documented known limitations.\n\nCLUSTER -> 2 fix-sites in verify_claims.py + 3 standalone bugs:\n- load_claims (188-228): WI-ruzib/INV-gobob (boundary-vocab), WI-fuhaf (root-shape), INV-zurih (YAMLError catch), WI-bopoz (field-name allowlist) = the META-jurig family.\n- verify_claim (246-256): WI-kajil (inconclusive-when-language-uncovered) -> then re-verify INV-bitig.\n- gitleaks.py: INV-pirad (no-op secret scan). sketch_embeddings.py: INV-dasig (HF network leak) + WI-jilik docs. taint.py match_sink: WI-razol (5541-FP false-VIOLATION cascade).\n\nPR SEQUENCE (preferred ordering for release-safety: false-CONFIRM before false-VIOLATION). NOT encoded as isbefore because these are independent fix-sites, not logical deps -- wiring them would falsely hide items from `tracker ready`.\n  PR1  INV-pirad   gitleaks stdin contract fix + NON-MOCKED known-positive smoke test (structural backstop for vendored-CLI contract breaks)\n  PR2  INV-dasig   HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 in _load_st_model_offline_first + WI-jilik env-var docs\n  PR3  META-jurig  ONE load_claims validation gate (WI-ruzib/INV-gobob + WI-fuhaf + INV-zurih + WI-bopoz)\n  PR4  WI-kajil    verify_claim inconclusive-when-language-uncovered; then re-verify INV-bitig\n  PR5  WI-razol    taint match_sink honor module qualifier + ambiguous_names (also fixes console-write net_send mis-route, F156.A1)\n  PR6  INV-hukug   reify claims-file-extras vs CLI-extras taint layers (INV-somut A.2 taint-loader hardening)\n\nREAL DEPENDENCY (wired as isbefore): WI-kajil -> INV-bitig. INV-bitig was closed by PR4 (020615f5) then REOPENED because the uncovered-language case escapes; it cannot return to satisfied until WI-kajil lands. WI-kajil's \"DEPENDS-ON WI-zavad\" tag is CONCEPTUAL ONLY -- the security fix makes verify-claims honest about coverage independent of fixing the JS analyzer.\n\nNOTES. ClaimVerdict.inconclusive + exit-code mapping (confirmed->0 / violated->1 / inconclusive->2) ALREADY EXIST (PR4 020615f5); PRs 3-4 EXTEND, not build. WI-kajil's coverage signal must come from analysis_runs (NOT limits.skipped_languages -- that field is itself broken, WI-nihir: setter has zero callers). After the arc lands, re-verify INV-somut / INV-murig (boundary face) / META-jurig with POSITIVE evidence; INV-fabov stays violated (spans config/search faces).\n\nOUT OF ARC (ship in 6.0.0 as known limitations): WI-nulot, WI-kikis (verify-claims output fidelity, P1); INV-murig config/search registry faces."  # 2f5d
